From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:26:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] feat(web): graphics pipeline (EGFX) per connection, and
 follow its resets

GNOME Remote Desktop requires the graphics pipeline ([MS-RDPEGFX]) and
closes connections that don't advertise it. The web client now registers
the EGFX channel (GraphicsPipelineClient, CAPVERSION_8 without H.264) when
the new `graphicsPipeline(true)` extension asks for it; it stays off by
default, as before.

EGFX servers answer a display-control monitor layout with ResetGraphics
rather than a deactivation-reactivation sequence. The session now resizes
the canvas to the new surface and fires the canvas-resized callback, so
live resize works against them.
